Title: Do not build a string from a null HOME when listing font folders
Repository: libresprite
Base: 89ea7597ed1d779e85c0019555f5b97c7eac22f0
Requires: preceding patches in series
Date: 2026-11-16
Author: aros-libresprite project
Problem: get_font_paths built a std::string from getenv("HOME"); with HOME unset that throws ("basic_string::_M_construct null not valid").
Change: Treat an unset HOME like an empty one.
Scope: all non-Apple, non-Android platforms
Upstream: candidate
Verification: Built for mainline AROS x86_64 (GCC 10.5, SDK nightly 20261110); LibreSprite starts on nightly 20261113 (pool v1-1, 2026-11-16)
Removal: When upstream handles an unset HOME.
---
diff --git a/src/base/fs_unix.h b/src/base/fs_unix.h
index 61b423a4ee0dfd547128f3ab8e38e51cff08d792..a7e442c262f3cfdda1c3647d9047c64afb77fe98 100644
--- a/src/base/fs_unix.h
+++ b/src/base/fs_unix.h
@@ -239,7 +239,8 @@ std::vector<std::string> get_font_paths()
 
 std::vector<std::string> get_font_paths()
 {
-    std::string home = getenv("HOME");
+    const char* homeEnv = getenv("HOME");
+    std::string home = homeEnv ? homeEnv : "";
     if (home.empty())
         home = "~";
     return {
